<BaseLayout
  title="Shipping Cost & Transit Time from China to Bahrain: Complete Landed Cost Breakdown (September 2026)"
  description="Shipping cost and transit time from China to Bahrain: Shanghai/Ningbo/Shenzhen to Khalifa bin Salman typical 22 days, 5% duty plus 10% VAT, and the CIF × 1.155 landed-cost formula with hidden destination charges."
  canonical={pageUrl}
  ogType="article"
  schema={schema}
>
  <div class="page-header">
    <div class="container">
      <Breadcrumb
        items={[
          { label: 'Middle East', href: '/middleeast/' },
          { label: 'Shipping cost & transit time China to Bahrain' },
        ]}
      />
      <span class="badge badge--amber">September 2026 updated</span>
      <h1>Shipping cost &amp; transit time from China to Bahrain: the complete landed-cost breakdown</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        The headline freight rate is only the first line. This page separates China-to-Bahrain ocean
        and air freight from THC, documentation, Bahrain clearance, inland transport and the 5% duty
        plus 10% VAT stack, then shows how the layers compound into a true landed cost — while
        keeping the typical 22-day transit window in view.
      </p>

      <section class="section container">
        <blockquote class="tldr">
          <p>
            <strong>TL;DR:</strong> Bahrain’s statutory stack is CIF ×1.155 (5% duty + 10% VAT), so a $10,000 CIF shipment adds $1,550 in duty+VAT — $525 more than the UAE/Oman ×1.1025 at $1,025. Khalifa bin Salman (BHKBS) is the only verified Bahrain sea gateway in the snapshot, with a 22-day typical transit and a 15–30 day range — a 15-day planning spread that makes the air leg a request-for-quote item because no Bahrain air transit number is published. Because Bahrain’s ×1.155 sits 5.25 points below Saudi’s ×1.2075 but 5.25 points above the UAE’s ×1.1025, King Fahd Causeway routing into Dammam/Riyadh is a congestion-and-inland-leg play, not a simple VAT win.
          </p>
        </blockquote>
      </section>

      <p class="small muted">
        Confidence badges separate verified rules from indicative market snapshots. Bahrain freight
        rates were not published in the verified snapshot, so every rate is shown as a
        request-for-quote marker. Treat every LOW-confidence figure as an indicative planning input
        and verify with your carrier before relying on it.
      </p>

      <div class="fact-grid mt-3">
        <div class="fact">
          <span class="fact-label">Baseline import duty</span>
          <span class="fact-value">5% CIF <ConfidenceBadge level="MEDIUM" /></span>
        </div>
